From 94fe954cada5199ae754054090c659c894d75da7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:42:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] selftests/bpf: cover ordered CPUMAP steering

Use live XDP test frames and generic XDP on loopback to exercise ordered
CPUMAP domains. A bounded TC receive gate holds the old target inside stack
delivery while another candidate is requested. Check that dequeue alone
cannot complete the old prefix and that full-queue drops return pending
reservations. Use single-packet test runs while gated: repeat > 1 changes
the XDP dispatcher and waits for an RCU grace period.

Cover discarded redirect requests, invalid interfaces, remote PASS/DROP,
rejection of second remote redirects, mixed native/generic batches,
parallel producers, entry replacement/deletion/recreation, missing targets,
and CPU offline/online with and without a concurrent producer. Recreate an
entry after CPU online to restore the worker's original CPU affinity.

Run serially because the fixture changes CPU online state. At least three
available CPUs are required. The 13 ordered subtests pass on a four-vCPU
x86-64 QEMU guest with CONFIG_RPS=n, KASAN and lockdep.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
---
